 17592186424042 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424049 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424043 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424049 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424049 1077 "selection" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424049 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424043 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424049 1079 #uuid "efac0da0-aee9-5e9c-ae73-a7e2c584348e" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424050 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424046 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424050 1069 "q-96334" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424050 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424050 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ compute $P(-2\\le X\\le 2).$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424050 1072 #uuid "2b0137dd-0ad1-53cf-acd8-0bbd632c8d90" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424050 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & -3\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2\\le X\\le 2) & =P(-2\\le X\\le 1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424051 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424047 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424051 1069 "q-130692" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424051 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424051 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ compute $P(W\\ge 1).$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424051 1072 #uuid "6a51ea05-5e14-5ec8-80f9-413f5ec71214" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424051 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 0\\le w\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\ge 1) & =P(1\\le W\\le 4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424052 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424049 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424052 1069 "q-96284" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424052 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424052 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ compute $P(U<-3).$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424052 1072 #uuid "b864ebe6-e085-5252-a91f-4ca0cb314e2f" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424052 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $U$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le u\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20},\\, & -10\\le u\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U<-3) & =P(-10\\le U<-3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}\\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-(-10)}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424053 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424048 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424053 1069 "q-96279" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424053 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424053 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ compute $P(W\\le 5).$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424053 1072 #uuid "b9258154-36aa-5bfe-9428-732732589876" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424053 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\le 5) & =P(3\\le W\\le 5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{5-3}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424054 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424045 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424054 1069 "q-96333" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424054 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424054 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ compute $P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424054 1072 #uuid "f0228a94-8a4a-532e-880c-3c74fb2a7fa3" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true] [17592186424054 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\pi },\\, & -\\pi \\le x\\le \\pi , \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-0)}{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534518 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0e3d93ec-eb09-56cb-a416-5e2e7bec5a82" 17592186424020 "answer-107d2581-115e-5fcf-a7ba-4b8a4e067792" 17592186424021 "answer-160a5126-2e24-5c1b-be6a-a06e49dea788" 17592186424022 "answer-19b9c547-b3de-5a3b-af9a-1d4bd21add26" 17592186424023 "answer-19f85468-debe-56c4-9c7b-72ce62714596" 17592186424024 "answer-1acc037d-bce5-53b6-8323-1b252862f034" 17592186424025 "answer-1e99867f-cfc9-54c7-b348-5f78d1c3d9fa" 17592186424026 "answer-25c1f749-943c-58ad-b0b0-8e9b295a57ad" 17592186424027 "answer-2e30620f-4add-5a5d-8a10-63fa89353160" 17592186424028 "answer-33ea49c6-ab8b-5f20-989d-636291cc3105" 17592186424029 "answer-3f1ef539-7e09-5084-96af-05c9d696698e" 17592186424030 "answer-3f72b617-3a2d-566c-9b4c-88d79b0fb5b9" 17592186424031 "answer-3feeccff-adf9-5ba7-9142-c8b271570281" 17592186424032 "answer-4538c02d-cc56-5357-9692-c45dbd1ff415" 17592186424033 "answer-51df5392-9584-5939-887e-e5eb023f5973" 17592186424034 "answer-534fce73-0f